This method requires some way of digging (pickaxe, wand) teleport and teleport
control.  It is not very common (for me, anyway) to get get both of the latter
two until a long way into the game.  What about the good ol' pickaxe method in
the spoilers?

Just dig 2 holes in the shop wall that are on the same vertical, horizontal or
diagonal line.  Drop unpaid goodies just in front of one hole, get in the hole
(you are now OUTSIDE the shop) and kick items off your goodies pile and out
the  other hole.  Then go pick them up!  Only problem is that breakables
(potions, mirrors, cameras) often break when kicked.  Anything else can be
stolen safely.

Here's a bad diagram:

--@-----     That's you standing in the hole in the wall at the top of the
|..x..@+     shop.  Notice how this hole is on the same diagonal line as the
|......|     one you have dug in the right side wall.  The space marked "x"
|......|     is where you drop the stuff you want to steal.
|......|
|......#
|......|
--------

A wand of digging will often dig both holes with one zap (from outside the
shop) and will always put them on the same line.

This method works because you are kicking from outside the shop (standing in
the wall is considered outside)  If you kick stuff out from inside, you get
charged for it.

To steal breakables, try to repeatedly steal and sell back some expensive
item (e.g. gems) until you have enough bucks to buy the breakable items.
This may not be much use in a potion shop where the shopkeeper may only 
want to buy potions off you.  You may also want to use this method to 
completely empty the keeper's pockets - they usually carry 2000 - 3000
zorkmids.  This is handy if a priest(ess) is in the dungeon.

I always use this method of robbing shops - it always works, you never piss
off the shopkeeper, never decrease your alignment (I think !?), and never
summon the Kops.

